cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the article."
# Add `doi:` (software DOI) here, and the article's Zenodo DOI under
# preferred-citation, once they are known.
title: "Coherence Before Symmetry: Lean formalization and numerical checks"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/gustafGitHub/oe-coherence-before-symmetry"
authors:
  - family-names: Ullman
    given-names: Gustaf
version: "1"
date-released: "2026-11-05"
abstract: >-
  Lean 4/mathlib formalization and seeded numerical checks accompanying the
  article "Coherence Before Symmetry: Positive Kernels, Random Frames, and
  Compatible Perspective Transformations" (version 1). Starting from finite
  block-matrix positivity in arbitrary dimension, the Lean libraries verify
  that maximal overlap forces positive comparison kernels to compose as
  unitary transformations, and that saturated homogeneous data over a finite
  group form a unitary representation. The 35-declaration axiom audit uses
  only standard logical axioms. The Python scripts check the triangle
  positivity criterion, defect and rank bounds, finite-group rounding, and
  the exact two-frame law.
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - positive kernels
  - unitary representations
  - Bargmann invariants
  - Gibbs measures
  - Lean 4
  - mathlib
  - observer equivariance
